      Copyright 2026 SG-WorkStation

      Original code in this directory is licensed under the MIT License.
      The complete text of the MIT License is provided in 'PCL.SGW/LICENSE',
      and applies together with the scope rules below. Its copyright notice
      and permission notice must be included in all copies or substantial
      portions of the Software, as the MIT License requires, so a copy of
      that file has to travel with any distribution of this directory.

      SPDX identifier for this path: MIT

      Scope of the grant, and how it meets the rest of the repository:

      (a) The MIT grant covers only original work authored by SG-WorkStation
          and placed in 'PCL.SGW/'. It grants no rights in any file outside
          that directory.

      (b) A file in 'PCL.SGW/' that is copied from, or is a derivative work
          of, code from another directory of this repository is not covered
          by the MIT grant. Such a file remains subject to the license of
          its source directory: the Apache License 2.0, or the custom terms
          in 'Plain Craft Launcher 2/LICENCE'. It must keep its original
          copyright and license notices, and must carry a prominent notice
          stating that the file was changed, as required by Apache License
          2.0, section 4(b).

      (c) Linking to, or depending on, code in the Apache-2.0 directories of
          this repository does not change the license of either side and
          does not place the MIT-licensed code under Apache-2.0. This
          follows the direction that permissive licenses allow: MIT-licensed
          code may be combined into an Apache-2.0 work, not the reverse.
          Consequently, Apache-2.0 code must not be copied into 'PCL.SGW/'
          and relabeled as MIT.

      (d) Distributing a build that combines several of these parts remains
          subject to every license involved: Apache License 2.0, section 4
          (retaining 'PCL.Core/NOTICE' and any other NOTICE text, marking
          modified files), and, for builds that include the application
          directory, the custom terms of 'Plain Craft Launcher 2/LICENCE'
          (naming, attribution, and no-charge distribution of verbatim
          copies of the unmodified software). The MIT grant above does not
          relax those obligations and grants no trademark rights.

