   4. MODIFICATIONS TO FILES UNDER THE DIRECTORIES ABOVE

      Copyright 2026 SG-WorkStation (modifications only)

      Editing a file does not change the license of that file. A file that
      SG-WorkStation modifies keeps the license of the directory it lives in,
      and the modified file is distributed under that same license.
      SG-WorkStation claims copyright in its own modifications; it does not
      claim ownership of, and does not purport to relicense, the pre-existing
      code.

      (a) Files edited inside 'Plain Craft Launcher 2/' remain subject to the
          custom terms in 'Plain Craft Launcher 2/LICENCE'. Its guide applies
          to distributed builds of the modified application.

      (b) Files edited inside the Apache-2.0 directories remain subject to the
          Apache License 2.0. Its section 4(b) requires a prominent notice
          that the file was changed, so every modified file should carry a
          line in its header, for example:

              // Modified by SG-WorkStation, 2026.

          Removing or replacing the original Apache header - for instance
          with an MIT header - would breach sections 4(a) to 4(c) of the
          Apache License 2.0 and is not what this map grants. Existing
          copyright and license notices stay in place; modification notices
          are added alongside them.

      (c) The reverse direction is permitted. Code from 'PCL.SGW/' may be
          copied into an Apache-2.0 directory, because MIT-licensed code may
          be incorporated into an Apache-2.0 work. The copy, as it then exists
          in that directory, is distributed under Apache-2.0; the original
          MIT grant continues to apply to the original copy.

      (d) A new file written by SG-WorkStation directly inside one of the
          directories above is original work authored by SG-WorkStation, and
          is distributed under the license of the directory it is placed in:
          Apache-2.0 in the Apache-2.0 directories, and the custom terms of
          'Plain Craft Launcher 2/LICENCE' inside that directory. Its
          copyright line credits SG-WorkStation alone.

